jobs.description:
Langan provides expert land development engineering and environmental consulting services for major developers, renewable energy producers, energy companies, corporations, healthcare systems, colleges/universities, and large infrastructure programs throughout the U.S. and around the world. Our employees collaborate seamlessly among 50+ offices and gain valuable hands-on experience that fosters career growth. Langan culture is entrepreneurial from advancing innovative technical solutions, to participating in robust training and knowledge sharing, to making progressive change within the communities we live and work.

Consistently ranked among the top ten “Best Firms to Work For” and Engineering News-Record’s top 50 firms worldwide, Langan attracts and retains the best talent in the industry. Employees thrive at Langan, a firm that fosters an inclusive and supportive work environment for all; prioritizes wellbeing, health, and safety; encourages volunteerism and philanthropy; offers workplace flexibility, along with carbon-neutral office spaces; and empowers individuals to contribute their skills and knowledge to make impactful contributions.

Job Summary

Langan is seeking a Project Environmental Engineer, Scientist, Geologist / Project Manager
to join its collaborative team in Pittsburgh, PA. This individual will serve a key function in developing and reviewing health and safety plans for technical project work, and verifying/validating that plans are adhered to through audits, field visits, and inspections. Manages tasks and projects and prepares proposals, technical documents, and reports. Develops project- and program-specific safety improvement plans.

Job Responsibilities

Demonstrates increasing competency in a combination of areas including field supervision, technical knowledge, and project management. Has a thorough understanding of the company’s policies and procedures specific to area of expertise;
Supports client contract-level health, safety, security, and environmental (HSSE) management, including monitoring of leading and lagging key performance indicators, assurance activities, capability-gap closure, and coordination with project managers, health and safety officers, subcontractors, and client stakeholders;
Supports contractor and subcontractor HSSE management, including prequalification and performance review; verification that contractual HSSE requirements are incorporated into project planning and flow down to subcontractors; and review of project-specific HASPs, risk assessments, JSAs/JHAs, training and competency records, incident and near-miss reporting, and corrective actions.;
Provides technical safety leadership for higher-risk or non-routine work and assists project teams in identifying competent personnel, required controls, mitigation measures, and review or approval requirements before work begins;
Develops task and project budgets and schedules and performs task and project administrative activities, including preparing progress reports and reviewing project billings;
Supervises field activities and conducts project-specific safety audits of Langan field staff and subcontractors. Responsible for making correct interpretations of findings. Ensures that data collection, field observations, and laboratory analyses are completed correctly, within budget, and on time;
Assists in planning schedules and developing task and project budgets. Prepares progress reports and draft change orders;
Performs and manages multiple projects and tasks within specific budgets, schedules, and deadlines. Monitors budgets, schedules, and project timelines. Minimizes write-offs by keeping projects on budget;
Prepares draft invoices, project billings, and assists in payment collections;
Demonstrates strong writing skills (organization, logic flow, grammar, clarity, appropriateness of word choice); can effectively organize, write and edit draft proposals, reports, and other documents;
Works with Staff and Senior Staff to improve efficiency and services performed. Provides direct oversight and management of Staff and Senior Staff for specific project assignments. Supervises, reviews, and approves work of Staff and Senior Staff;
Coordinates other work groups within the same or different office locations and/or within the same or different disciplines on an as-needed basis;
Knowledgeable in all Langan services for internal coordination and cross-selling purposes;
Maintains a thorough understanding of the company’s policies and procedures, as well as the methods and procedures specific to area of expertise;
Applies standard practices and techniques to unusual situations or to devise new approaches to problems. Recognizes inconsistent or inappropriate results; knows when to consult with others regarding problem resolution or taking appropriate action;
Participates in interviewing and hiring staff;
Coaches, trains, and motivates staff assigned to projects;
Participates in the identification and pursuit of new clients, prepares proposals, learns to develop additional work within existing projects, and attends business development meetings with new and existing clients;
Communicates clearly, effectively, and professionally with clients, contractors, subcontractors, staff, project personnel, supervisors and others. Actively participates in internal and external technical presentations and produces written articles for internal and external publications;
Demonstrates a strong commitment to customer service and responsiveness to client needs;
Masters effective public speaking skills. Assists in preparing and giving client and other professional group presentations and participates in client meetings;
Stays current on engineering practices, guidelines, regulations, and best management practices and attends internal training to expand knowledge and skills;
Recommends new approaches and ideas that continuously improve efficiency and services performed;
Member of professional engineering or technical society;
Actively participates in internal Health and Safety training and has a strong commitment to Health and Safety in the workplace and field;
Manages or assists with managing staff; and
Performs other duties as requested.

Qualifications

Bachelor’s degree in Civil/Environmental Engineering or Science;
Master’s degree with Safety Management emphasis a plus;
PE or PG licensure if applicable;
Certified Safety Professional (CSP);
6-10 years experience;
Strong understanding of regulatory requirements;
Strong attention to detail;
Strong customer service skills and responsiveness to client needs;
Ability to multi-task effectively;
Excellent analytical and judgment capabilities;
Ability to work well individually and within groups;
Effectively manage multiple clients and projects;
Ability to develop and manage project budgets;
Ability to coach and assist with the management of staff;
Strong written and verbal communication;
Effective public speaking skills;
HAZWOPER training, maintenance of annual physical and respirator fit test, and annual 8-hour HAZWOPER re-certification;
OSHA Construction Safety and Health 30-Hour;
OSHA General Industry Safety and Health 10-Hour;
Radiation Safety Officer;
Rail Car Incident Response;
Demonstrated experience implementing HSSE management systems and supporting contractor assurance, competency verification, subcontractor oversight, risk control, incident learning, performance reporting, and continuous improvement for industrial or energy-sector projects;
Ability to occasionally work hours during evenings and weekends, when needed;
Ability to travel and spend all day at a jobsite or client office; and
Must have a valid driver’s license.

Langan provides a rich array of programs and benefits to help its employees advance their careers and enhance the quality of their lives. Our comprehensive compensation package includes: full-time employment company paid medical, dental, and vision coverage; life insurance, short- and long-term disability insurance, and paid pregnancy disability leave; 401(k)/Roth with company match; paid time off including parental and military leave; employee referral and professional license bonuses; and educational reimbursement.

Langan offers employee resource groups; flexible work schedules; extensive training; wellness programs; buddy and mentoring programs; and much more!

Langan is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all qualified applicants and employees, including individuals with disabilities and protected veterans. We believe that an inclusive workplace is essential for the well-being and success of our employees.

Please review our Applicant Privacy Notice at Collection to understand how we collect, use, and retain your personal information: https://www.langan.com/langan-notice-at-collection

